course: dictionary
lesson: 8987
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Sitting is a good example: it can mean resting on a seat, staying in one place, or a time when a meal is served. The words around it are the clues that show which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Two minutes of sitting still can feel like the hardest thing ever.» Here sitting still means keeping your body still while you rest on your seat. The word still is the clue.
explain: «The book was sitting on the shelf» does not mean the book is resting on a chair. It means the book stayed in its place. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Sitting means resting your bottom on a chair, the floor or another seat, with your back up.
fact: Sitting can also mean staying in a place or position, as in «the book was sitting on the shelf».
fact: A sitting is one time a meal is served to a group, or one session of doing something. Phrases like «at one sitting» mean all in one go.
fact: In the UK, a «sitting-room» is a living room, a small, pretty room where people sit and relax.
fact: «Sitting still for hours stiffens the back and neck.» Getting up and moving often is good for you.
exercise: «Two minutes of sitting still can feel like the hardest thing ever.» What does sitting still mean here? | Running very fast | *Resting on a seat without moving | Falling over | Sitting on a boat in the sea
exercise: «The book was sitting on the shelf.» What does sitting mean here? | Writing a story | A meal served to a group | Resting your bottom on a chair | *Staying in one place
exercise: «Mole is now writing plain, simple ones in the blue boudoir (a small, pretty sitting-room).» What is a sitting-room? | A bedroom with a big bed | A shed in the garden | A kitchen for cooking | *A room to sit and relax in
test: «Sitting still for hours stiffens the back and neck.» According to the text, what helps more? | *Getting up and moving often | Lying down on the carpet | Sitting still for even longer | Sitting in a special chair
test: Ben finished the whole cake «at one sitting». What does at one sitting mean? | *All in one go, in one session | Over a long time, on different days | Without a plate | Sitting on the floor while he ate
exam: Which sentence uses sitting to mean staying in a place? | «Sitting still is hard for me.» | «She is sitting in the chair.» | «The sitting room is cosy.» | *«The cup was sitting on the table.»
